ountered this title i  figured that somewhere roon balant would  have been able to get at least  one sympathizer to her cause this time  that special person is ichisei  an orphan who works as a prize fighter  in the cutthroat city of lux making a  living as a fighter isn't easy  which he experiences first hand as an  incident causes him to lose his limbs  however just like our previous  protagonist ichise would find himself  safe from the jaws of death through the  power of science  this time he finds himself working  heavily with one of the factions  fighting for control over the city  and he encounters ron a girl who has the  power to see the future  together the newly formed duo worked  together in order to prevent the worst  possible  ending a huge faction war that would  crush the city for good  this is early 2000s mad house in action  and as you can see some of their style  has carried over through the decades i  generally like mad house adaptations and  technologies no exception  however i've got to warn you the series  can be rather slow in pace compared to  what the premise will make you believe  nonetheless it's still a good watch and  i find it quite similar to the next  title on the list  while technolise is a very niche title  ergo proxy  certainly isn't so what we've got here  is one of the most beloved and complex  psychological mysteries that the anime  industry has to offer it says a lot when  it stood the test of time and remains  quite popular despite  one not being a mainstream big three  shonen and two not being a  childhood anime fondly remembered by the  people entering the age of 30 now ergo  proxy takes us to the post-apocalyptic  world where the last of humanity have  taken refuge in the city of romdo while  there are no titans to keep people  inside the cities the planet outside is  just as uninhabitable thus humanity has  adapted to life with humanoid robots  called auto revs of course  things go horribly wrong and these  robots contract 